From bd9be0d13eeb0027765e231ef674bd66bc6869ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:07:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Pitch: a shortlist of seven, one seen switch, a question
 for a missed film (rules 1700-1702)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Build 38, owner-approved journeys/b62b-pitch-shortlist ii and b64-pitch-clarify-and-seen.
- rankRecut returns at most PITCH_SHORTLIST (7) films, never padded; signed in, films under
  65% shown match are left out (fewer than three clearing it: the best there are, with a note).
- unseen/seenOk/rewatch become query.seen ("new" | "either" | "rewatch") plus loved (the
  "Ones you loved" chip); old stored and cached queries migrate (migrateSeen). The count line
  reads "7 films · New to me ▾" with the small menu; op "rank" takes `seen`. No seen chips.
- No 422 "Didn't catch that": a film we couldn't find asks "Which film did you mean?" (close
  titles via lib/search-typo.ts, "Skip it, just Korean films"); nothing read asks "What are you
  in the mood for?". "Films like Korean Parasite" reads Parasite + Korean. "Just show me both"
  only for two readings; a chosen clarify pill takes the select blue.
- The anchor chip reads "Like <film>"; Tonight's "New to Me" is "New to me".
- Web and iPhone (Recut.swift not compiled here); docs, invariants, battery and DS log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
