+- **2026-11-12 · Pitch: a shortlist of seven, a 65% match floor, one seen switch, "Korean Parasite" read as Korean** (rule 1700, rule 1701, rule 1702; build 38)
+- **Before → after:** (1) `rankRecut` returned `opts.limit ?? 24` films; now `PITCH_SHORTLIST` (7), only as many as fit, never padded. (2) Signed in with a profile there was no shown-match floor on Pitch (rule 1119's `MATCH_FLOOR` 55 stored only drops films while 24 others remain); now the first 24 of the order get their canonical match and a film under 65% SHOWN (`shownMatch`, lib/taste/shown-match.ts) is left out (no match yet: kept; "so bad it's good": exempt); when fewer than 3 clear it, the best there are show with a plain note. (3) `unseen` / `seenOk` / `rewatch` became `seen: "new" | "either" | "rewatch"` and `loved`. New to me and Either rank exactly as the old default and `seenOk` did. Rewatch without Ones you loved is new: every film the viewer has seen is the pool, lifted by the old comfort-rewatch bonus (rating and age) so loved films lead; Ones you loved is the old `rewatch` (4.5★+ or hearted, warmth up, bleakness down). The friend's seen films are left out when "new" is set in so many words (typed, or picked on the count line), as `unseen` did. (4) The keyword parser and the model's anchor drop a leading language word ("Korean Parasite" → anchor Parasite, language ko; "French Kiss" kept whole). (5) An anchor that does not resolve is no longer a "Not used" word: the route asks "Which film did you mean?" with up to three typo-close titles (lib/search-typo.ts over lib/top-titles.ts) and ranks the rest of the ask.
+- **Why:** owner-approved build 38 Pitch changes (journeys/b62b-pitch-shortlist ii, b64-pitch-clarify-and-seen): a real shortlist, not 24 rows; nothing under 65% for a known viewer; one seen switch; "Didn't catch that" turned into the question.
+- **Measured:** scripts/pitch-battery.ts on the 2026-11-12 fixture (catalogue snapshot, outside the repo), signed out: 168/168 on origin/main, 176/176 here (the 168 plus 8 new asks: Korean Parasite, Japanese Spirited Away, an unknown title with and without a close match, gibberish, three seen-switch asks), graded now on the seven shown instead of the top 10, no case lost. The floor (`--floor`, three accounts' stored `user_film_score` from the 2026-11-06 fixture, each account's seen films left out, ordered by `orderForViewer` on the stored match, first 24 read): of 173 asks that rank, asks under three films for some account 1 before, 3 after (the new two: "Telugu comedy" and "Telugu comedy on Netflix", 5 → 2, 5 → 2 and 5 → 0); ask-account pairs under three 3 → 9 of 519; mean shortlist 6.94 → 6.87. So few asks thin out that the fallback (the best available with the note) only meets those. Not measured: the canonical match (the fixture's scores are the stored rows of 2026-11-06, before rule 1593's top flatten, which only moves numbers above 85 and so never crosses 65); the model path (no key offline); a Rewatch list's order on real libraries. scripts/test-recut-parser.ts 33/35 before and after (the two failing cases are the same pre-existing rule 1178 ones), with the new nation and seen cases passing; scripts/test-recut-rank.ts unchanged except the chip label ("Like Heat").
+- **Who it affects / data touched:** every Pitch answer (web and iPhone): at most seven films; signed-in viewers lose films under 65% shown. Stored `recuts.query` rows and cached parses with the old flags are read through `migrateSeen`; nothing stored was rewritten. The parse cache key stays `recut:parse:v4` (the old flags still read).
+
 - **2026-11-12 · AI features get kill switches and daily call caps; the batch label crons get a day budget and pause on a spike day** (rules 1630, 1631; launch cost guard)
 - **Before → after:** every gated Claude call passed only the day's dollar budget ($11), the per-user $1, the anonymous 2,000 and the 60,000 backstop (rule 740). Now `reserveClaudeCall(label)` first checks the feature's kill switch (`AI_PITCH`, `AI_WHY`, `AI_READS`, `AI_GROUPS`, `AI_SHELVE`, `AI_LABELS`, `AI_OTHER`; default on) and, after the dollar checks, a per-feature daily call cap (why 950, reads 1,650, groups 300, other 200; Pitch, shelve and the catalog crons keep their own caps). The batch passes (label-backlog, label-traits, new-release-themes), which were bounded only per run, now share `DAILY_CLAUDE_CRON_USD` ($5 of estimated spend a day), are cut to fit what is left, and send nothing while `AI_LABELS` is off or the day's user budget is spent. Prompts, models, label values and every threshold that produces data are unchanged.
 - **Why:** launch prep, 2026-11-12: a traffic spike must not be able to run up a surprise bill.
